BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4a8e3919-b2c2-49eb-bbcd-102d9aa5aec0
DTSTAMP:20260223T190325Z
DTSTART:2026-03-05T00:30:00+00:00
DTEND:2026-03-05T01:30:00+00:00
SUMMARY:Free Food @ ACM - Meeting #7, Movie Night: The Internet's Own Boy (2014)
DESCRIPTION:<p>Join the ACM for a movie night, where we'll be watching&nbsp;<em>"The Internet's Own Boy (2014)",&nbsp;</em>a documentary about&nbsp;programming prodigy and information activist Aaron Swartz. *<em>Note: An RSVP is required, for pizza ordering purposes.</em></p>
<p>Movie Description: "He<em> helped develop the Internet Protocol RSS and was a co-founder of Reddit. Chronicling his pioneering efforts crusading for open access and free speech and the resulting legal nightmare and tragedy that ensued, The Internet's Own Boy is a dynamic and moving portrait of a brilliant tech millionaire who renounced the values of Silicon Valley startup culture and used technology to tirelessly fight for social justice, no matter what the cost."</em></p>
<p><strong>Perks:</strong></p>
<p>- Fun Technology Movie</p>
<p>- Pizza</p>
<p>- ACM</p>
LOCATION:Julian Hall, Room 31
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7c636f63-bc0c-4a41-9b7c-21e3983c7365
